---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Socials from '../components/Socials.astro';
import { SITE, PERSON_ID, WIKIDATA_ID } from '../consts';

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'What does Charlie Linville do?',
    a: 'Charlie Linville is a co-founder of Updraft Consulting, an AI consulting firm working with clients in mortgage and healthcare staffing, and the founder of Guleki, an app publisher building AI-native mobile products. He also builds AI agents, quantitative trading systems, and security tooling.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where is Charlie Linville based?',
    a: 'Denver, Colorado. He studies Applied Mathematics, Engineering & Physics at the University of Wisconsin–Madison and spent a semester abroad at the University of New South Wales in Sydney, Australia.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is Charlie Linville building right now?',
    a: 'Updraft Consulting, Guleki, and Sizzle Roasting Software — a platform that runs a coffee roastery end to end with closed-loop machine control and AI roast coaching.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I contact Charlie Linville?',
    a: `By email at ${SITE.email}, or through LinkedIn, GitHub, or X.`,
  },
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    '@id': `${SITE.url}/about#page`,
    name: 'About Charlie Linville',
    url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
    mainEntity: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${SITE.url}/about#faq`,
    mainEntity: FAQ.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Base
  path="/about"
  title="About Charlie Linville — AI Engineer & Founder in Denver, Colorado"
  description="Charlie Linville is an AI engineer and co-founder of Updraft Consulting, based in Denver, Colorado, studying Applied Math, Engineering & Physics at UW-Madison."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title">About Charlie Linville</h1>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          I'm Charlie Linville — an AI engineer and founder based in Denver, Colorado,
          studying Applied Mathematics, Engineering &amp; Physics at the University of
          Wisconsin–Madison. I build AI systems and the businesses around them.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm working on</h2>

        <p>
          I co-founded <strong>Updraft Consulting</strong> in June 2026, an AI consulting
          firm with paying clients in mortgage and healthcare staffing. My work there spans
          both engineering and sales: I architected seven AI workflows for a mortgage
          brokerage — everything from contract date extraction through refinance targeting —
          and built a GLBA-aligned data-handling framework that classifies client data by
          sensitivity and maps each class to an approved processing environment. Regulated
          industries can't adopt AI without that groundwork, and most consultancies skip it.
          I also co-lead sales, scoping and pitching engagements to presidents and review
          committees at firms up to $1B in revenue, and I've run live AI training for 34
          professionals — every person surveyed left with a workflow they could actually use,
          and 83% asked to expand the engagement.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'm also the founder of <strong>Guleki</strong>, an app publishing company focused
          on AI-native mobile experiences. Our first product, Geolocate Me, gives AI
          assistants real-time location context through a private GPS tracker with Model
          Context Protocol integration. It's live on both iOS and Android.
        </p>

        <p>
          Most recently I've been building <strong>Sizzle Roasting Software</strong>, which
          runs a coffee roastery end to end — bean inventory and costs, live machine control,
          and AI roast coaching. It steers the roaster automatically to hit a target
          temperature curve, predicts how a batch will taste from its roast data, and listens
          for first crack through a microphone, retraining itself on each machine's own audio.
          A 47-tool agent built on Strands and LangChain runs local models on an NVIDIA Jetson
          to keep coaching responses under eight seconds.
        </p>

        <h2>Before this</h2>

        <p>
          From September 2025 to March 2026 I was co-founder and technical lead
          at <strong>Agori</strong>, an early-stage fintech startup. I architected and shipped a
          real-time quantitative paper trading platform in fourteen weeks using AI-native
          development workflows, then deployed it for a trading competition run with Old
          Mission Capital at the University of Michigan. I owned AWS infrastructure, security,
          developer tooling, and CI/CD, recruited four team members, managed three direct
          reports, and supported an angel raise while leading product strategy.
        </p>

        <p>
          Before Agori I consulted for <strong>SC Sports</strong>, where I built the auction
          pricing system behind two live deployments — 2,800 lots priced, each converted into
          a max-bid recommendation against an ROI target, with buyer's fees and bid multipliers
          encoded for eighteen different auction houses. Earlier, from 2023 to 2024, I worked
          with <strong>Backpack Society</strong>, a nonprofit serving more than 70 schools
          supporting kids in unstable food situations. I architected and pitched a systems
          overhaul, won funding from the leadership team, rebuilt the organization's website on
          AWS at 45% lower cost, and advised the board on technology selection and budgeting.
        </p>

        <p>
          My technical roots go back further than that. From 2020 to 2024 I competed
          in <strong>CyberPatriot</strong>, the national cybersecurity competition run by the
          Air Force Association, leading Cisco networking for my school's team and finishing 12th
          nationally against more than 5,000 teams.
        </p>

        <h2>School and research</h2>

        <p>
          I'm pursuing a BS in Applied Mathematics, Engineering &amp; Physics (AMEP) at
          UW–Madison, graduating in 2028, with coursework in Modern Physics, Numerical Linear
          Algebra, Mathematical Computing, and Philosophy of AI. I spent the first half of 2026
          studying abroad at the University of New South Wales in Sydney, Australia.
        </p>

        <p>
          Outside of coursework I'm part of the Wisconsin Quantum Computing Club, where I
          competed in the 2024 IBM Fall Fest hackathon and took home both Community Favorite
          and First to Finish. I've simulated neutral-atom qubits in QuTiP, built time-dependent
          Hamiltonians for ground-to-Rydberg drives, and trained a neural network that detects
          local and non-local errors in a 12-qubit system at 95%+ accuracy. From October 2024
          through December 2025 I served as a Member At-Large on the UW–Madison Vice Chancellor
          for Finance &amp; Administration Study Group, selected through the Associated Students
          of Madison shared governance process, advising senior university leadership on food
          security, budget model changes, and renewable energy.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>

        <p>
          The thread running through all of it is systems: figuring out how the pieces fit,
          where the leverage is, and what actually has to be built versus what merely sounds
          impressive. I lean heavily on AI-native development workflows, which is how a
          fourteen-week production trading platform was possible at all. I care about shipping
          things that survive contact with real users and real regulators.
        </p>

        <p>
          When I'm not building, I'm roasting coffee — which is how Sizzle started — watching
          Formula 1 for the engineering as much as the racing, training for longevity, and
          reading.
        </p>

        <h2>Common questions</h2>

        <dl class="faq">
          {FAQ.map((f) => (
            <>
              <dt>{f.q}</dt>
              <dd>{f.a}</dd>
            </>
          ))}
        </dl>

        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <Socials />

        <p class="meta-note">
          This is the Charlie Linville who builds AI systems — catalogued on Wikidata
          as <a href={`https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/${WIKIDATA_ID}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{WIKIDATA_ID}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
